oncretely (infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json, .env, MCP_CLIENT_PAT_*, infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md)"],"finding":"The repo-root local-only client-credential config TEMPLATE and the real gitignored file it renders to are referenced but never given concrete paths/filenames, yet the guard AC asserts '.gitignore matches the gitignored real credential path' and 'the template with a placeholder passes'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc6504a4e4dcee8b2","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach bullet 3 + AC 'The gitignored real credential path is matched by .gitignore'","norm_id":"ne80b510dba7fbf0c","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor must choose the template filename and the gitignored render target path, and the .gitignore pattern, without a stated decision"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"State e.g. template `mcp-client-credentials.example.toml` (committed) rendering to `mcp-client-credentials.local.toml` (gitignored via an explicit `.gitignore` line), and reference these exact paths in the guard AC.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the edits required to make `infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json` rsync-excluded AND gitignored: add a new `--exclude` entry to `autodeploy.sh` RSYNC_EXCLUDES (line ~163) and a matching pattern to `infra/.gitignore` (currently only `compose/.env`), or choose a path already excluded/ignored.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'emits the tokens JSON the verifier reads (`infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json` ...)' and AC: 'both files are gitignored (NOT under the rsync'd tree)'","autodeploy.sh:163-164 RSYNC_EXCLUDES = (--exclude '/.git' --exclude 'infra/compose/.env' ...) — no tokens-json exclude; infra/compose/ is otherwise rsync'd (docker-compose.yml lives there and is a BOT_PATH)","infra/.gitignore:16 = 'compose/.env' only — no entry for a tokens JSON under compose/","Contrast: the existing rsync-excluded secret (`.env`) is the ONLY infra/compose path excluded, so a sibling JSON is NOT excluded by default"],"finding":"The plan asserts the materialized tokens file `infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json` is 'gitignored (NOT under the rsync'd tree)', but the code facts show it would fall INSIDE the rsync'd tree and would NOT be gitignored unless new edits are made that the plan does not enumerate. `autodeploy.sh` RSYNC_EXCLUDES (lines 163-164) excludes only `infra/compose/.env`; the rest of `infra/compose/` (including `docker-compose.yml`) is rsync'd. `infra/.gitignore` (line 16) ignores only `compose/.env`. To make the tokens JSON both rsync-excluded and gitignored as claimed, the plan must add (a) a new RSYNC_EXCLUDES entry in `autodeploy.sh` and (b) a new pattern in `infra/.gitignore` — neither is named as an edit target.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f744cd30edc3a11c4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Transform bullet + AC 'materialize' oracle ('both files are gitignored (NOT under the rsync'd tree)')","norm_id":"nb928cbfa00c696fe","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Deploy rsyncs infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json from the repo/source tree over the on-box materialized copy, or a materialized secrets file lands inside the synced tree","An operator or CI commits the rendered tokens JSON because it is not gitignored, defeating the never-commit-a-secret guarantee"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add `--exclude 'infra/compose/mcp-static-tokens.json'` to autodeploy.sh RSYNC_EXCLUDES and add `compose/mcp-static-tokens.json` to infra/.gitignore, and name both as edit targets in the plan's edit-set/file_impact.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how a blank per-client slot is represented in mcp-static-tokens.json — OMIT the record for any client whose MCP_CLIENT_PAT_* is unset/empty (so _parse_static_record never sees an empty token_env), and state the intended behavior when ALL slots are blank (_load_static_tokens raises 'defines no tokens' and the verifier fails to start), reconciling this with the beb1 'file always exists' guarantee.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_parse_static_record: token_env 'names env var ... which is unset or empty' -> AuthConfigError (_mcp_auth.py:764-767)","_load_static_tokens: 'if not by_digest: raise AuthConfigError(... defines no tokens)' (_mcp_auth.py:724-725)","mcp_server.py:631-633 'the verifier is constructed (so a bad config still fails closed at startup)' — construction failure crashes the process","The cited beb1 precedents (rebar-bot-signing-key, opcert-ed25519-key) are single opaque files whose emptiness is a benign per-service fallback, NOT a multi-record JSON that a strict parser rejects wholesale (fetch-secrets.sh:99-138)"],"finding":"The plan asserts the tokens JSON is 'ALWAYS created even when a slot is blank' but does not specify what the file CONTAINS for a blank slot; if a token_env record is emitted for a client whose MCP_CLIENT_PAT_* env var is unset/empty, _parse_static_record raises AuthConfigError, which per mcp_server.py fails the WHOLE verifier/MCP server at startup (not just that client), and an all-blank file trips _load_static_tokens' 'defines no tokens' raise.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f410bb9651c0a8439","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section, 3rd bullet ('The tokens file is ALWAYS created even when a slot is blank (bug beb1...)') and AC materialize oracle ('the tokens file is created even when a slot is blank (beb1)')","norm_id":"n18b53af8d6ee82fa","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Only copilot's PAT is provisioned in SSM; codex/claude slots blank — emitter writes 3 token_env records — verifier __init__ raises on the first empty var and the entire rebar-mcp server fails to start (all clients locked out).","First-boot / all slots blank — tokens file exists (satisfies beb1) but _load_static_tokens raises 'defines no tokens', crashing the server."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have fetch-secrets.sh emit a token_env record ONLY for each client whose MCP_CLIENT_PAT_* value is non-blank (still always writing the file for beb1), and add an oracle: a file with some-blank / all-blank slots either loads the provisioned subset or fails closed as documented — not a partial-slot crash of the whole verifier.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"high","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State fetch-secrets.sh's failure behavior for the per-client PAT materialization: SSM fetch error surfaces loudly (non-zero exit / logged), and the .env + tokens JSON write is atomic (temp-file + rename) so a failed run cannot leave a partial token set the verifier reads.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'fetch-secrets.sh materializes each per-client PAT from SSM into the on-box container env source' — the SSM read is a new external failure point","The plan handles the blank-slot case (beb1) but not an SSM fetch error or a partial/interrupted materialization write","This follows the existing opcert-guard.map.conf pattern, so error handling may be inherited — but the plan does not say so"],"finding":"fetch-secrets.sh adds a new SSM fetch (external call + file I/O) for the per-client PATs, but the plan only specifies the blank-slot degradation (beb1: always create the tokens file). It does not state what happens when the SSM/aws call itself fails or errors (auth failure, network, throttling) mid-materialization — whether the step fails loudly (surfacing the error) or silently leaves a stale/partial .env, and whether the write of .env + tokens JSON is atomic so a failed run can't leave the verifier reading a half-written token set.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5700270dc4ca9dc5","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale / Acceptance Criteria (materialize oracle)","norm_id":"nd95aafe4dad82a6e","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":fal